-- title:
--   Integral lift of level-N modular functions over a number field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an integer $N \ge 1$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, and assume $q \nmid N$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ that is finite over $\mathbb{Q}$, and write $R := A \cap K$ for the subring `NodeLocalized.coeffSubring A K` of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with $\mathrm{red}_K : R \to k$ the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$ along $R \subseteq A$. Let $h_0$ be a Laurent series with coefficients in $R$ and let $\bar g$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, the subfield of $k(\!(X)\!)$ generated over $k$ by $j_k := X^{-1} \cdot \overline{jNum}$ and by its image $j_{k,N}$ under the substitution raising exponents by the factor $N$. Assume that applying $\mathrm{red}_K$ coefficientwise to $h_0$ gives the series $\bar g$, and that $\bar g$ is integral over the $k$-subalgebra of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` generated by $j_k$ and $j_{k,N}$. Then there are a Laurent series $y$ over $R$ and an element $g$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` — the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\!(X)\!)$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull N` $\subseteq \mathbb{Q}(\!(X)\!)$ — such that the series $g$ is the coefficientwise image of $y$ under $R \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the coefficientwise image of $y$ under $\mathrm{red}_K$ is $\bar g$, the series $g$ lies in `NodeLocalized.fieldOver N K`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\!(X)\!)$ generated by the constant series attached to elements of $K$ together with $j_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ and $j_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}},N}$, and $g$ is integral over the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subalgebra of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` generated by the images of $jq$ and of its $N$-fold exponent substitution under the coefficient embedding $\mathbb{Q}(\!(X)\!) \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\!(X)\!)$.
--
--   This is the level-$N$ lifting step for functions with coefficients in a number field: integrality over the affine coordinate ring $k[j,j_N]$ in characteristic $q \nmid N$ is lifted, together with the prescribed $q$-expansion modulo $\mathrm{red}$, to an element of $K(j,j_N)$ integral over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[j,j_N]$, combining good reduction of the modular curve with descent of coefficients from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to $K$. It feeds the analysis of prolongation tuples at places of the special fibre, where integrality of residues of such lifted functions is used.
